// REJECTS: Field 'specification' is required
//
// `specification` and `auth` are both REQUIRED on a RelationalDatabaseConnection, and both
// are optional as far as the grammar is concerned -- the definition rule is a bare
// `(store | type | auth | specification | ...)*` with no cardinality at all.
//
// Everything that makes this connection well-formed is therefore invisible to a generated
// parser: it will accept a connection with nothing but a store, and the first sign of
// trouble is a null datasource at execution time. Note the ordering of the checks, too --
// this reports the missing specification, not the missing auth.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::NoSpec
{
   store: fixture::neg::Db;
   type: H2;
   auth: DefaultH2;
}
